      title: 'Sugar industry paid Harvard scientists to point at fat',
      text: `The Sugar Research Foundation paid three Harvard nutritionists about US$6,500 (roughly US$50,000 today) for a 1967 NEJM review that played down sugar's role in heart disease and blamed fat. It set the review's goal and saw drafts. The funding wasn't disclosed. Internal documents surfaced in 2016.`,
