      title: 'Big diet trial left unpublished for 40 years',
      text: `The Minnesota Coronary Experiment (9,423 people, 1968–73) swapped saturated fat for corn oil. Cholesterol fell, but deaths didn't: each 30 mg/dL fall in cholesterol came with a 22% higher risk of death, and the oil group did worse among people over 65. The full results stayed in a basement until 2016. Seed-oil critics cite it; others note the short follow-up and the margarines used.`,
